 "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which is the best estimate for 52.2 + 20.97?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "options": [{"t": "83", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "730", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "63", "ok": false, "fb": "Not quite – work through the method again."}, {"t": "73", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}]}, {"id": "m6u08s1m17", "type": "num", "prompt": "A plank is 13.58 m long. 3.47 m is cut off. How long is the rest?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10.11, "unit": "m", "units": ["m"], "tol": 0, "errs": []}, {"id": "m6u08s1m18", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find the missing number: 7.28 + ☐ = 13.2", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5.92, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u08s1m19", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 5.9 + 6.76 − 2.28.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10.38, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true}, {"id": "m6u08s1m20", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Sam writes 8.2 + 0.45 = 1.27. What is the right answer?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "reason": "8.20 + 0.45 = 8.65.", "options": [{"t": "9.65", "ok": false, "fb": "Check by estimating."}, {"t": "8.65", "ok": true, "fb": "Correct."}, {"t": "1.27", "ok": false, "fb": "He lined up the last digits instead of the decimal points."}]}], "notes": "v3"}, {"id": "8.2", "title": "Adding and subtracting fractions", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "idea", "t": "When can I add fractions straight away?", "p": ["Only when they have the **same denominator**. Then add the numerators and keep the denominator: 2/7 + 3/7 = 5/7.", "The denominator tells you the **size** of the parts; you can only add parts of the same size."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "What if the denominators are different?", "p": ["Change the fractions into **equivalent fractions** with a **common denominator** – a common multiple of both denominators, ideally the lowest.", "1/3 + 1/4: multiples of 3 and 4 meet at 12. 1/3 = 4/12 and 1/4 = 3/12, so 1/3 + 1/4 = 7/12."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "How do I work with mixed numbers?", "p": ["Add or subtract the **whole numbers** and the **fractions** separately, then combine: 2 1/5 + 1 3/5 = 3 4/5.", "If the fraction part becomes improper, change it to a mixed number: 1 3/4 + 2 2/4 = 3 5/4 = 4 1/4.", "If you cannot take away the fraction parts, exchange 1 whole: 3 1/4 − 1 3/4 = 2 5/4 − 1 3/4 = 1 2/4 = 1 1/2."]}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I add or subtract fractions with different denominators?", "p": ["Step 1: Find the lowest common multiple of the denominators.", "Step 2: Write each fraction as an equivalent fraction with that denominator.", "Step 3: Add or subtract the numerators; keep the denominator.", "Step 4: Simplify, and change improper fractions to mixed numbers."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Different denominators", "p": [], "q": "Work out 5/6 − 1/4.", "steps": [["LCM of 6 and 4 = 12", ""], ["5/6 = 10/12, 1/4 = 3/12", "× 2 and × 3"], ["10/12 − 3/12 = 7/12", ""]], "a": "7/12"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Exam-style: mixed numbers", "p": [], "q": "A path is 2 1/2 km and another is 1 2/3 km. How far are they together?", "steps": [["Wholes: 2 + 1 = 3", ""], ["1/2 + 2/3 = 3/6 + 4/6 = 7/6 = 1 1/6", ""], ["3 + 1 1/6 = 4 1/6", ""]], "a": "4 1/6 km"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Adding the denominators", "p": ["1/3 + 1/4 is **not** 2/7. Adding the denominators changes the size of the parts. Use a common denominator."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Simplify at the end", "p": ["Always check if your answer can be simplified (6/8 = 3/4) or written as a mixed number. Many mark schemes ask for the simplest form."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 300, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "8.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 1, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u08s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 1/4 + 1/2. Give your answer 